  "groundingSupports": [
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 170,
        "endIndex": 422,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [3]: Mistral AI raises €3B Series D led by Samsung at €21B+ valuation**\n* **What is confirmed:** Mistral AI officially announced a €3 billion Series D funding round at a post-money valuation exceeding €21 billion (~$24 billion)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 424,
        "endIndex": 531,
        "text": "The round was led by Samsung Electronics, with co-leads Scaleup Europe Fund (managed by EQT) and PSG Equity"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 533,
        "endIndex": 622,
        "text": "Additional investors include BlackRock, Luxembourg, ASML, Nvidia, and Andreessen Horowitz"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2,
        3,
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 624,
        "endIndex": 701,
        "text": "This represents the largest private tech equity fundraise in European history"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 703,
        "endIndex": 857,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** The company is utilizing funds to build out proprietary data center infrastructure and scale compute capacity alongside model R&D"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 859,
        "endIndex": 979,
        "text": "Dollar-denominated valuation figures in secondary reporting vary slightly (~$24B) due to daily currency conversion rates"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1101,
        "endIndex": 1362,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [11]: Anthropic walks away from $6B acquisition of Decart AI**\n* **What is confirmed:** Bloomberg reported that Anthropic terminated talks to acquire Israeli AI chip-efficiency startup Decart for approximately $6 billion following due diligence"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6,
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1364,
        "endIndex": 1478,
        "text": "Decart develops software aimed at reducing inference/training compute costs and improving semiconductor efficiency"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        8,
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1480,
        "endIndex": 1612,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** Story relies on unnamed sources familiar with the matter; both Anthropic and Decart declined formal comment"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6,
        9
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1614,
        "endIndex": 1738,
        "text": "Reporting indicates the two companies may still pursue commercial or technical collaboration without an outright acquisition"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        8,
        7,
        9
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1867,
        "endIndex": 2129,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [5]: Huawei investing in Chinese lithography suppliers to bypass export limits**\n* **What is confirmed:** The *Financial Times* reported that Huawei is taking a hands-on project management role in China's domestic semiconductor tool supply chain"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10,
        11
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2131,
        "endIndex": 2318,
        "text": "Huawei is making direct and indirect investments in lithography startups—notably Yuliangsheng—and facilitating deals with major fabs like SMIC to test domestic immersion DUV equipment"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10,
        12
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2320,
        "endIndex": 2397,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** Based on anonymous industry and supply chain sources"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2399,
        "endIndex": 2533,
        "text": "Huawei has publicly denied formal corporate affiliation with entities like SiCarrier/Yuliangsheng, despite technical and team overlaps"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2535,
        "endIndex": 2692,
        "text": "Domestic DUV tools remain in early validation stages and are estimated to be several years away from high-yield commercial volume production parity with ASML"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        12,
        13,
        14
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2848,
        "endIndex": 3175,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [13]: Grindr settles UK privacy lawsuit for £26 million**\n* **What is confirmed:** Grindr disclosed in SEC filings (Form 8-K) and formal announcements that it reached a £26 million (~$34–$35 million) settlement in a High Court group action lawsuit in England and Wales brought on behalf of ~12,000 UK users"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        15,
        16,
        17
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3177,
        "endIndex": 3336,
        "text": "The lawsuit alleged that prior to 2020, Grindr unlawfully shared sensitive user data—including HIV status and test dates—with third-party ad-tech platforms"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        15,
        18
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3338,
        "endIndex": 3433,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** The settlement contains no admission or finding of liability by Grindr"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        19,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3435,
        "endIndex": 3532,
        "text": "Grindr emphasized that the claims cover pre-2020 practices under former owner Beijing Kunlun Tech"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        19,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3534,
        "endIndex": 3612,
        "text": "Payouts will occur in two £13 million tranches (December 2026 and March 2027)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        15,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3756,
        "endIndex": 3977,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [4]: Arm debuts Neoverse CSS N4 semi-custom compute platform**\n* **What is confirmed:** Arm officially unveiled its Neoverse CSS N4 (\"Ranger\") semi-custom compute subsystem platform for cloud data centers"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        20,
        21
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3979,
        "endIndex": 4144,
        "text": "Fabricated on TSMC's 3nm N3P node, it supports between 8 and 128 Neoverse N4 cores per die at up to 3.8 GHz, featuring PCIe Gen 6/7, CXL 4.0, and DDR5/LPDDR6 support"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4146,
        "endIndex": 4328,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** Performance claims (such as 2x socket performance and 1.25x performance-per-watt improvement over CSS N3) are based on Arm's internal architecture benchmarks"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        20,
        22
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4513,
        "endIndex": 4829,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [16]: Google-backed space startup Pixxel raises $100M Series C**\n* **What is confirmed:** Indian Earth-observation startup Pixxel announced a $100 million Series C funding round co-led by Temasek and Seraphim Space, with participation from Google, Radical Ventures, 360 ONE Asset, and IMM Investment"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4831,
        "endIndex": 4889,
        "text": "Total capital raised by the startup stands at $195 million"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        23,
        26
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4891,
        "endIndex": 5098,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** The capital will fund Pixxel's expansion from hyperspectral hardware satellites into broader planetary software intelligence (\"Aurora\") and higher-resolution satellite constellations"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        27,
